# Innovation Research & Development AI System (NamoNexus)

NamoNexus (NRE v5.0.0 "Sovereign Fortress") is a distributed cognitive operating infrastructure designed for autonomous scientific research, persistent semantic reasoning, and enterprise-grade multi-agent coordination. It replaces single-shot AI Q&A with a full research pipeline: planning → parallel hypothesis generation → peer critique → recursive reflection → contradiction analysis → coherent synthesis — all backed by a five-tier persistent memory stack (Qdrant, Neo4j, PostgreSQL, Redis, and cross-session `ResearchMemory`). The system is deployed via Docker Compose with FastAPI on the backend and a React/TypeScript dashboard on the frontend, connected by Server-Sent Events (SSE) for real-time cognitive streaming.

The platform operates on strict architectural boundaries: every agent action is mediated through a `RuntimeEventBus` (or distributed `RedisEventBus`), every message is evaluated by a `PolicyEnforcer` before execution, and every step is recorded in an immutable `ReasoningTrace`. Multi-tenancy with PostgreSQL Row-Level Security, JWT authentication, sliding-window rate limiting, and Cognitive FinOps quota tracking make NamoNexus production-ready for enterprise SaaS deployments. The system runs fully in heuristic mode without any external LLM or database dependencies, gracefully degrading as services become available.

