### MemoryAgent (Reactive) — Asynchronous Persistence

`MemoryAgent` is a `ReactiveSubscriber` that runs in the background listening exclusively to the event bus. On `hypothesis.generated` it indexes to Qdrant; on `synthesis.ready` it writes to PostgreSQL, sets Redis TTLs, and pushes nodes to Neo4j. Zero blocking of the core agent execution loops.

```python
from src.agents.memory_agent import MemoryAgent
from src.memory.qdrant_connector import QdrantConnector
from src.memory.neo4j_connector import Neo4jConnector

qdrant = QdrantConnector(host="localhost", port=6333)
neo4j = Neo4jConnector(uri="bolt://localhost:7687", user="neo4j", password="password")

memory_agent = MemoryAgent(
    event_bus=bus,
    qdrant=qdrant,
    neo4j=neo4j,
    db_session=async_session
)

# MemoryAgent registers its own subscriptions — no explicit calls needed
await memory_agent.start()  # Runs reactively in background

# Internally handles:
# bus.subscribe("hypothesis.generated") → qdrant.upsert(chunk)
# bus.subscribe("synthesis.ready")      → postgres.insert(HypothesisRecord)
#                                       → redis.setex(trace_key, ttl=86400)
#                                       → neo4j.merge_node(synthesis_node)
```

